randtip_1=Enemy vehicles, installations and objectives can be hacked by approaching the entity and pressing (and holding) the Interact button.
randtip_10=Skill point accrual can be accelerated through the use of active and passive boosters available on the market.
randtip_11=Militia items require no skills to use, but are less efficient, requiring more PG/CPU than comparable items.
randtip_12=Each dropsuit has a unique slot configuration and limited PG/CPU that is used up as you fit weapons, equipment and modules. Advanced and prototype dropsuits have more slots than lower tier suits.
randtip_13=Vehicle modules are either active or passive; passive modules are always on, while active modules must be turned on/off manually using the module switch.
randtip_14=A single item of everything used in a spawned fitting is depleted every time you die. Fittings become invalid if you run out of one or more items used in the fitting. Blueprints are not consumable and will never run out.
randtip_15=Some modules have a stacking penalty – using multiple modules of the same type reduces the effectiveness of each subsequent module. Check the description in Show Info to be sure.
randtip_16=Most AUR items have lower skill requirements than the ISK variants so if you don’t have enough skill points you can use AUR to get early access to them.
randtip_17=All weapons affect armor and shields differently. Hybrid weapons are equally effective against shields and armor. Explosive weapons are weak against shields, but very effective against armor. Laser weapons are very effective against shields, but weak against armor. Projectile weapons are slightly less effective against shields than armor.
randtip_18=Target intel illustrates how efficient your current weapon is against the shields/armor of the target you're aiming at. If you're outmatched you should consider retreating and finding another target.
randtip_19=Every handheld weapon has an operation and proficiency skill. Training these will give you an edge over your opponent in battle.
randtip_2=Multiple people hacking simultaneously will complete the hack faster!
randtip_20=Using the nanite injector to revive downed teammates saves your team a clone.
randtip_3=Hacked objectives enter a ‘contested’ state during which time they can be hacked back to prevent switching alignment to the opposing side.
randtip_4=Scan precision determines the fidelity of a scan; the lower the number the more precise the scan is.
randtip_5=Every dropsuit, vehicle and installation has a scan profile that determines how easily it can be detected by scanning equipment and modules; the higher the number the easier the entity can be detected.
randtip_6=Hide from enemy scanners by using modules to reduce your scan profile.
randtip_7=Skills must be purchased from the market before they can be used.
randtip_8=Skill points are used to upgrade the level (1-5) of any skill you have already purchased and activated.
randtip_9=Skill points are accrued passively over time as well as through excellence on the battlefield; the greater your contribution to the team in a battle, the more skill points you earn.
reload=RELOAD
skirmishtext=Two teams vie for control of a designated planetary location by destroying the enemy Mobile Command Center (MCC) in the area while protecting their own. By capturing and maintaining control of NULL cannon installation components, a team is able to increase the amount of damage done to the enemy MCC. The more NULL cannons held, the faster the enemy MCC takes damage. The battle is over when one of the MCCs is destroyed.
