[Hud_Subtitles_Minmatar]
Minmatar1=Once a thriving tribal civilization, the Minmatar were enslaved by the Amarr Empire for hundreds of years.
Minmatar2=Most were freed after a great rebellion, but only at a tremendous cost.
Minmatar3=Today, the Minmatar Republic is a strong, resurgent nation, determined to win back the glory of its past.

[Hud_Subtitles_Tutorial]
NPEsub00001=Welcome, soldier
NPEsub00002=You are about to jump into a galaxy of opportunity, wealth, destruction, and death.
NPEsub00003=If you are adequately prepared,
NPEsub00004=you are far less likely to die violently on the battlefield.
NPEsub00005=Your war begins long before the first shot is fired.
NPEsub00006=The equipment you choose,
NPEsub00007=including your dropsuit, weapons and vehicles,
NPEsub00008=will determine not only your odds of survival,
NPEsub00009=but also your role on the battlefield.
NPEsub00010=This equipment must be purchased from the marketplace,
NPEsub00011=and will not be returned to you should you lose consciousness, or life, in battle.
NPEsub00012=Your clone continually accrues skill points in battle and out.
NPEsub00013=In turn, these points are applied to skills to increase their effectiveness,
NPEsub00014=or to teach you how to use more advanced gear.
NPEsub00015=The skills you train will define the warrior you ultimately become.
NPEsub00016=Your Neocom is as important a tool as any weapon you will ever wield on the battlefield.
NPEsub00017=It provides remote access to the market;
NPEsub00018=allows you to customize combat fittings;
NPEsub00019=plan your skill progress;
NPEsub00020=communicate with other mercenaries;
NPEsub00021=and most importantly,
NPEsub00022=tracks all ongoing ground combat in the cluster.
NPEsub00023=Your mercenary status allows you to fight for the corporations or factions of your choice.
NPEsub00024=Once committed to a battle,
NPEsub00025=you will join your allies in an orbiting war barge to suit up,
NPEsub00026=form squads, compare gear
NPEsub00027=and devise strategies for the battle ahead.
NPEsub00028=Remember that communication extends beyond the mercs around you.
NPEsub00029=You can discuss tactics both in a local chat and within your corporation,
NPEsub00030=and even with starship pilots in EVE Online.
NPEsub00031=Combat in New Eden is fast, frantic, and brutal.
NPEsub00032=As good as you are,
NPEsub00033=you will die! And when you do,
NPEsub00034=you will reawaken in a clone ready to return to battle,
NPEsub00035=wiser and better prepared for the challenges ahead.
NPEsub00036=Whether sneaking past enemy positions,
NPEsub00037=plowing through them in a tank,
NPEsub00038=or supporting your squad,
NPEsub00039=you must adapt to a dynamic and dangerous battlefield.
NPEsub00040=Tactical objectives change with every battle.
NPEsub00041=You might need to clear out drone infestations
NPEsub00042=or participate in massive land-grabs sponsored by galactic empires.
NPEsub00043=You may find yourself fighting wars for ideals, for money,
NPEsub00044=or simply because it’s what you are good at.
NPEsub00045=Along the way you’ll meet like-minded mercs and forge alliances.
NPEsub00046=Because one day,
NPEsub00047=the land you're fighting for could be your own.
NPEsub00048=Your teammates don’t need to be your best friends,
NPEsub00049=but you will need to trust them and work together as a unit.
NPEsub00050=Being in the same squad will improve your combat effectiveness.
NPEsub00051=And having a starship pilot join you can provide substantial benefits,
NPEsub00052=including orbital strikes on your enemies.
NPEsub00053=DUST 514® is more than a chance to lay down blistering fire,
NPEsub00054=rush over terrain in armored vehicles,
NPEsub00055=and fight across the galaxy alongside your fellow mercs.
NPEsub00056=Every battle, every action, every decision you make,
NPEsub00057=will bring the galaxy together or tear it apart.

